{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/307302-pacts-and-blood-bonds","id":307302,"title":"Pacts and blood bonds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-09T03:54:22-08:00","id":307302,"title":"Pacts and blood bonds","content":"When one of my players asked me a question in regards to pacts and blood bonds I stumbled a bit. Now wanted to ask here if I'm on the right track or not:<br /> * If a demon makes a pact with another being that is blood bonded to a vampire and wants to take the blood bond for one of his covers (for whatever reasons) <br /> that I ruled so far is possible (thus the demons cover is now blood bonded to the vampire instead of that other mortal).<br /> <br /> * Now the question is on the opposite way:<br /> a.) Could a demon grant a vampire a blood bond via pact (thus that someone becomes blood bond to that vampire<br /> b.) Could get the demon the blood bond from the vampire (regnant).....aka the demons cover becoming the regnant of the blood bond in question<br /> <br /> with those two I'm not sure. Theoretically b is possible (but it interferes with that the demon cant take the vampire template out of a pact I think). A I'm <br /> even more unsure if possible or not than b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T06:54:22-08:00","id":307377,"title":"","content":"demons can take aspects from someones life. You can take &quot;rich&quot; from someone but it doesn't mean that the demon now has the money in the bank. Just people will see him as rich. if he took the blood bond people would think he is bonded but he is not.<br /> <br /> demons can give people things, money, friends skill. he can not give a blood bond. A pact doesn't change a person's emotions. A demon can't make a moody awful wife/husband for a person great. The demon could change the wife/husband life as in they are rich if that was what made them not fun to be around. But doesn't give emotion control. He can not make someone feel the effects of the blood bond. The demon could let a vampire or even the mortal to think they are blood bound but magical effects would not be there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T08:24:37-08:00","id":308228,"title":"","content":"Had someone help me translate (sick currently so not top thinker).<br /> If we get you correctly it is so: A is bloodbound to B. C makes a pact with B so that he gets the bloodbound of his with A. The effect is then as follows:<br /> * A is still bloodbound to B<br /> * A THINKS he is bloodbound to C, although he will find out quite fast as soon as he thinks about / meets B that he is bound to B.<br /> <br /> OR is it so<br /> * A is no longer bloodbound to B<br /> * A THINKS he is bloodbound to C and reacts accordingly but there is no longer a magic compulsion thus if C hurts A or tries to command A around A will get it fast that there is no longer a compulsion to stay in &quot;love&quot; with C","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T17:24:25-08:00","id":308661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/307302-pacts-and-blood-bonds#post307302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When one of my players asked me a question in regards to pacts and blood bonds I stumbled a bit. Now wanted to ask here if I'm on the right track or not:<br /> * If a demon makes a pact with another being that is blood bonded to a vampire and wants to take the blood bond for one of his covers (for whatever reasons)<br /> that I ruled so far is possible (thus the demons cover is now blood bonded to the vampire instead of that other mortal).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow it, although I think in a strict reading of rules-as-written it can't be done \u2014 demons can't exchange supernatural aspects through pacts (check the corebook, pacts section on pacts with supernatural beings). But in the case of the demon exchanging a condition imposed from without, as an aspect of cover to suffer himself? That sounds more interesting to allow than to disallow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/307302-pacts-and-blood-bonds#post307302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a.) Could a demon grant a vampire a blood bond via pact (thus that someone becomes blood bond to that vampire<br /> b.) Could get the demon the blood bond from the vampire (regnant).....aka the demons cover becoming the regnant of the blood bond in question</div> </div> </div> </div>These I would not allow. A demon can't rule a blood vinculum because the demon doesn't <i>have</i> the supernatural power of the vitae to impose one. a) is more plausible, but without the exchange of cover conditions complicating the situation, it feels too easy and pat to make up for its interesting aspects to me, so I would rule closer to rules-as-written myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T04:43:59-08:00","id":308946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/307302-pacts-and-blood-bonds?p=308228#post308228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had someone help me translate (sick currently so not top thinker).<br /> If we get you correctly it is so: A is bloodbound to B. C makes a pact with B so that he gets the bloodbound of his with A. The effect is then as follows:<br /> * A is still bloodbound to B<br /> * A THINKS he is bloodbound to C, although he will find out quite fast as soon as he thinks about / meets B that he is bound to B.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah this works, I would go this way with a mix game where the vampire still has power over the mortal but the mortal doesn't even know. Still the mortal would act devoted to the demon as the memory is still there but it would kind of be like realising slowly you have fallen out of love with somone (if you can call the blood bond love). They would still be addicted to vampire blood though and the demon can feed the adiction, not that the mortal knows that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/307302-pacts-and-blood-bonds?p=308228#post308228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OR is it so<br /> * A is no longer bloodbound to B<br /> * A THINKS he is bloodbound to C and reacts accordingly but there is no longer a magic compulsion thus if C hurts A or tries to command A around A will get it fast that there is no longer a compulsion to stay in &quot;love&quot; with C</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is what I would go with. So all the emotions the person had are appiled to the demon. But from the pact onwards the bond would be gone. As it was the demon that feed the person blood,but as it was the demon who blood the mortal had all this time now blood has no effect. Even though the bond is now gone though again I would rule the person is still addicted. If the demon feeds the person his blood there might be a placebo effect where the person think they are getting what they need but the next scene they need vampire blood more than ever.<br /> <br /> If the demon had addictive presence exploit then I might rule they can make a few for ever level of blood bond the victim had. Not RAW but it has simlar effect. I say I might rule as this is something I would think over for a while (more time than it will take to make this post at least).<br /> <br /> Here is something to think about though, imagine doing this to a person who would be dead if it wasnt for the blood, they are 130 years old. You take the bond and reality changes. The demon doesnt have the power of blood, so the mortal dies when he was meant (50 years ago) to but the demon's cover also has been feeding to someone for over 50 years blood who now is dead. Feeding a person blood who is not alive to be fed is a cover breach if I know one. Cover crashes because of a paradox. I would give a compromise roll with at least a -3 penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T12:18:49-08:00","id":309386,"title":"","content":"Blood Bonds are very much a different supernaturals bailiwick, so I would not let a Demon mess with them. If Demons can just give Blood Bonds more easily then Vampires something is wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator 